 down to ~1.6%, Ujjivan raised it to **1.8-2.0%**, cut FY27 credit-cost guidance to **0.9-1.0% of average assets** and lowered planned opex to **6.4% of average assets** — on the back of MFI annualised slippages halving (2.68% → 1.72%), Bucket-X collection efficiency holding at 99.68% and a borrower base that grew for the first time after seven quarters of contraction. Q1 delivered ROA 2.2% / ROE 18.2% with the secured book crossing the halfway mark (50.4%) at 42.7% YoY growth, so the FY27 question shifts from \"can they earn\" to whether the deferred ₹250cr capacity-building spend and deposit-side pricing pressure claw back the beat over H2.","trig":[]},"lm":"2026-07","m":13673,"mem":1,"pdd":"2023-10-03","prev_stage":3,"prev_zone_vpe":2.0,"r":37.6,"s":"UJJIVANSFB","sig":"Advancing (S2)","sx":{"SMA_50":"65.6","base_count":"","drawdown_from_prev_signal":"","duration_from_prev_signal":"","pct_below_52w_high":"5.0","pct_change_from_prev_signal":"","pivot_close":"","pivot_low":"","stage_changed_since_prev_signal":"","vpe_df_60d_sum":"1.5","vpe_zone_cumul_df":"-0.5"},"t":""}},"s":"UJJIVANSFB"}